# ============================================================
# Netlify redirects — https://docs.netlify.com/routing/redirects/
#
# Legacy WordPress URLs. The old WP Engine site served the legal
# pages at these paths; index.html links to /privacy.html and
# /terms.html. These 301s keep the old links (and their search
# ranking) working once wifisquared.com is pointed at Netlify.
#
# Verified live on the WP site 20260729:
#   /privacy-policy/                        -> the privacy policy
#   /terms-of-service/                      -> 301s to the line below
#   /terms-of-service-and-return-policy/    -> the terms page
# ============================================================

/privacy-policy                       /privacy.html   301
/terms-of-service-and-return-policy   /terms.html     301
/terms-of-service                     /terms.html     301

# internal/ holds working drafts — the FCC label data, the label generator,
# and the unpublished network management disclosure. Netlify publishes every
# file in the repo, so these are explicitly 404'd. An unreviewed policy draft
# reachable by URL is a liability even when nothing links to it.
#
# The trailing ! is load-bearing. Without it an existing file shadows the rule
# and Netlify serves the file instead of the redirect — verified: these paths
# returned 200 until the force flag was added.
/internal/*                           /404.html       404!
